# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing matching these patterns may
# ever be committed. Local notes with IDs, passwords or connection strings stay
# on disk and out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*id and pass*
*password*
*secret*
*credential*
.env
.env.*
*.pgpass
pgpass.conf
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data. The extract is ~45 GB and lives on D:, never in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.csv
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
_manifest.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated per run. scripts/build_uat_notebook.py rebuilds this notebook on
# every UAT pass with that run's probe token baked in, so committing it would
# be churn. The generator is the source of truth and is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
notebooks/zz_uat_capacity.Notebook/
uat_capacity.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fabric Git integration syncs the workspace into fabric_ws/. A SQL database
# item exports one file per database principal, named after the principal, so
# the account UPN ends up in both a filename and a CREATE USER statement with
# its SID. This repository is PUBLIC. Keep the whole Security folder out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
fabric_ws/**/*.SQLDatabase/Security/

# Build output of the architecture diagram. index.html is the deliverable and is
# tracked; template.html is an intermediate and a second full copy of the page.
architecture-diagram/template.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The film. The source is the work and is tracked. These are not:
#   node_modules  ~300 MB of dependencies
#   .capture      Playwright's raw webm, deleted by capture_arch.py anyway
#   out/stills    frame-by-frame renders used to review layout before a render
# out/           every render. the master is 62 MB and a git history is the
#                wrong place for it. video/poster/ carries the poster frame,
#                which is what the README needs.
# public/arch.mp4 IS tracked: it is an input to the build, not an output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
video/node_modules/
video/.capture/
video/out/stills/
video/out/*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT MINE. "ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM ANON/" is client material that happens to sit
# in this working tree as a reference. This repository is PUBLIC. It must never
# be committed, so it is ignored by name rather than left to a careful `git add`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM ANON/
